THE DATA IS NOT MIT LICENSED. READ THIS BEFORE COMMERCIAL USE.

The MIT grant above covers the source code in this repository only.

`data/looming.npz` is derived from the FlyWire FAFB v783 connectome, which is
released under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). That licence follows the derived file, so the packaged
subnetwork -- and therefore any deployment of the connectome detector that
uses it -- is **non-commercial use only**, and redistribution must be under
the same terms with attribution.

In practice, for a robot:

  * research, teaching, coursework, portfolios and hobby projects: fine;
  * a commercial product: not with this data file. The code is yours under
    MIT, but you would need to obtain connectivity data under terms that
    permit commercial use, or contact the FlyWire team.

The `flow` baseline controller uses no connectome data at all and is
unencumbered by this clause.

Cite: Dorkenwald et al., "Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain",
Nature 634, 124-138 (2024). https://codex.flywire.ai
